"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including the preoperative PSA of 6.9 and the pathological T3a stage with extraprostatic extension documented post-surgery. A countervailing finding is that surgical margins were negative, and seminal vesicle invasion was absent. The absence of nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Biopsy findings (Gleason 3+4) align with the prostatectomy specimen grade (Gleason 3+4). Prognostic revision would be significantly aided by postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory. The current data lacks information on any prior systemic therapy, which could impact risk stratification. The fixed estimated horizon is 69.39 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 45.11–93.68 months; its coverage has not been validated."
